course: dictionary
lesson: 930
title: Blind: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it tell you which meaning is right. «Behind one drawn blind they see the shadow of a bird-cage.» Here a blind is the cover pulled down over a window to keep out light.
explain: «Picture a blind woman walking to the shops: her guide dog stops dead at the kerb.» Here blind means not able to see. Try it in the sentence: "a not able to see woman" is odd, but "a woman who cannot see" makes sense, so this is the meaning.
explain: Blind can also be a verb, a doing word. «The bright light blinded me.» The light stopped me seeing for a short time. Blind can also mean not noticing something, as in blind to his mistakes.
explain: Think of a word with many meanings like a coat that can be worn in different ways. Read the whole sentence, find the clues, then swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
fact: Blind has several meanings, so always check the sentence to find the right one.
fact: «Blind» can mean not able to see.
fact: To blind someone is to stop them seeing, for a short time or for ever.
fact: A blind is a covering you pull down over a window to keep out light.
fact: Blind to something means not noticing it, as in «blind to his mistakes».
exercise: «Behind one drawn blind they see the shadow of a bird-cage.» What is a blind here? | A person who cannot see | A bright light | *A covering pulled down over a window | A kind of bird
exercise: «The bright light blinded me.» What does blinded mean? | Made me hear a noise | Made me laugh | Made me hungry | *Stopped me seeing, for a short time
exercise: Dad says he is blind to the dust on the shelf. What does blind to mean? | Afraid of it | *Not noticing it | Able to see it very clearly | Wanting to clean it
test: «Picture a blind woman walking to the shops.» What does blind mean? | Very angry | *Not able to see | Not able to walk | Lost in a shop
test: Jo says a blind is a cloth on the window. Is she right? | No, a blind is a bird | No, a blind is a person | *Yes, it keeps out light | No, a blind is a white cane
exam: Which sentence uses blind as a verb? | Picture a blind woman walking to the shops | *The bright light blinded me | Behind one drawn blind they see a bird | Bats are not blind
